# Machine-specific settings for the scheduled jobs (launchd on macOS).
#
# Copy this file to scripts/ops.local.env and edit it. The real file is
# gitignored; the copy is what ships with the repository.
#
# Every value here overrides the default that bin/ops_env.sh computes. Nothing
# in this file is secret: the credentials live in the database and in the
# keychain, not here.
#
# OPS_PYTHON    — interpreter to use. Default: <checkout>/.venv/bin/python,
#                 else ~/ops-dashboard/.venv/bin/python, else python3.
# OPS_DATA_DIR  — the folder holding ops.db. Default: <checkout>/data if it
#                 holds an ops.db, else ~/ops-dashboard/data. Setting it
#                 explicitly is what keeps a job writing to the live database
#                 instead of to the checkout.
# OPS_LOG_DIR   — where the job logs are written. Default: ~/ops-dashboard/logs
#                 if it exists, else <checkout>/logs.
# OPS_CONFIG_PATH   — path to config.json (provider keys, defaults).
# OPS_SECRETS_DIR   — folder for the secrets store when the keychain is off.
# OPS_DISABLE_KEYCHAIN=1  — use OPS_SECRETS_DIR instead of the macOS keychain.
#
# OPS_PYTHON=/Users/you/ops-dashboard-live/.venv/bin/python
# OPS_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/ops-dashboard/data
# OPS_LOG_DIR=/Users/you/ops-dashboard/logs
